invariant: INV-41
file: rsa_ifma_sign.c
catches: proof/prove-one.sh rsa_ifma_sign_setup
reason: state_finish's array holds a prime's largest word count and not
  the word above it, which digits_to_words writes and the subtraction
  reads, so at that count both pass the array's end. The rsa_ifma_sign_setup
  proof runs state_finish at every prime word count the build admits, the
  largest among them.

--- old
    uint64_t words[RSA_IFMA_SIGN_WORDS_MAX + 1];
    digits_to_words(words, mod->words, s->power, s->modulus.digit_count);
--- new
    uint64_t words[RSA_IFMA_SIGN_WORDS_MAX];
    digits_to_words(words, mod->words, s->power, s->modulus.digit_count);
